# the record's machine artifacts never enter git.
# var/ — scratch: probe output, captures, anything ephemeral. The
#   honesty law's "ephemeral artifacts delete themselves" starts here:
#   if it is disposable, it lives under var/ and git never sees it.
# *.new — the upgrade plan's conflict copies: your words were kept and
#   the refreshed scaffold rides beside them. Resolve or delete; never
#   commit.
var/
*.new
